    "raw_text": "\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt. The prompt asks for \"a 15-second, 9:16 vertical video in a 3D animation style depicting an adult female ship crew member wearing a dark blue/navy jacket, standing on a ship deck with a white flag, backlit by warm golden hour lighting, with a calm sea and clear sky.\" \n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\nThe overall visual quality is moderate (score 3). The frames show decent resolution and clarity, but there are occasional minor softness or compression artifacts that prevent a higher rating. Lighting remains generally consistent with warm backlighting, though some frames exhibit slight exposure variation. The ship, water, and sky render plausibly, and the flag movement reads as natural; however, the sequence lacks standout visual polish.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\nAlignment to the prompt is strong (score 4). All major elements are present: a female figure on a ship deck, wearing a navy jacket, a white flag, backlit warm lighting, a calm sea, and a clear sky. The framing is close to the requested vertical orientation, and the scene adheres to the described setting. Minor deviations may exist in exact pose timing or framing across frames, but they do not significantly detract from alignment.\n\nPhysical Consistency / Common-sense:\nPhysical consistency is moderate (score 3). The scene generally respects basic physics: the flag moves with wind, the ship appears buoyant, and lighting/shadows are coherent. However, there are subtle inconsistencies in motion dynamics or environmental interactions that prevent a higher score.\n\nOverall assessment:\nThe video demonstrates solid technical execution with good alignment to the prompt, but the visual quality and physical consistency are only moderate. The final scores align with Visual Quality: 3, Text-to-Video Alignment: 4, Physical Consistency: 3.\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 3\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 4\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 3\n"
